WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
Google just built an ai that notices your friend's birthday and suggests a perfect gift from your own photos and calendar. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 167. Here's something that's going to change how the apps on your phone finally start earning their keep. Google Labs just launched Dream Beans, a new artificial intelligence experience that stitches your digital life into one spot. Artificial intelligence or ai is software that spots patterns and information,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:56.580
and then writes or draws from those patterns. Dream Beans gathers details from Gmail, Calendar, Search, Gemini, and Google Photos. Gemini is Google's Chatbot app, the place where you already type questions and get answers. On Photos, it can use face grouping, which sorts pictures of the same person into piles, like splitting a yearbook by classmate. It might even build a one-of-a-kind illustrated story of you and a friend named Beth.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:23.080
Think of it like a really thoughtful pal who remembers tiny details so you never have to repeat yourself. Those stories show up as one daily notification inside the app, not an endless scroll. Compare that to TikTok or Instagram, where the feed never stops and you keep swiping. This is more like a single sticky note on your locker, written just for you that morning. If one catches your eye, you tap it to see extra details and direct links.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:39.140
That link might be a movie trailer or a place to buy a suggested gift. Everything is opt-in, which means the system waits for your yes, like an RSVP before anyone puts you on a guest list. You stay in charge with a thumbs-down button when a suggestion misses the mark.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:02:08.860
That thumbs-down is like telling a pal, nah, that is not my vibe, so they learn what you actually care about. Strict privacy filters sit in front of the whole thing, like a locked diary where you hold the only key. Those filters keep your data from being used without your permission. For students and teens, that can mean less time hunting for ideas and more time acting on nudges that already feel personal. For parents, it is a way to keep family moments organized without downloading yet another app.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:26.280
The real shift is that your own information starts working for you in one place, instead of sitting locked in separate services. Picture ingredients trapped in different kitchen cabinets, never meeting in one pot. Dream Beans is the moment those cabinets open and dinner actually gets cooked.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:35.100
You can try the first version today by finding Google's announcement on X and joining the Dream Beans waitlist, or the app when it opens to you.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:50.120
Want the part that made this click for me? Your phone already knows a dentist visit because the calendar and the reminder tools pass notes to each other. Dream Beans stretches that same idea across more of your stuff at once, but only after you switch it on.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:03:03.660
Once it is on, the AI quietly scans the connected apps for matching dates or matching names. That is like a group project where every classmate brings one folder and someone finally spreads all the pages on one table.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:15.560
When it finds a match, it builds a short story tile, a little illustrated card about that person or that moment. Maybe it remembers a fun photo of you two from last year and weaves that into the card.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:24.120
Then it waits. It does not dump a pile of links on you until you tap, which is the same courtesy as knocking before you open a bedroom door.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:34.780
After the tap, you can see more options, including those links. The important habit is this. It can show you what it used so you can correct it if something feels off.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:42.140
You are not watching a magic trick. You are watching your own puzzle pieces click together with you still holding the box lid.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:50.660
If you can picture classmates sharing folders, then a card getting made, then a knock before extra links, you already understand the loop.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:56.660
That loop is simpler than the hype makes it sound, and you did not need a computer science class to follow it.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:10.000
While that idea is still bouncing around, there is a phone update you can actually install today. Apple released iOS 27, the new software that runs iPhones, and Siri now has its own dedicated app.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:16.300
Siri is the voice assistant built into iPhones, the one you ask to set timers or send texts.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:30.040
The update also brings fresh icons, plus separate volume controls for system sounds and alarms. Think of two knobs on a stereo, so a quiet alarm does not get blasted by the same speaker that plays your game music.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:36.000
Apple says the update brings big performance improvements that make the phone feel faster overall.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:41.860
It works on phones all the way back to the iPhone 11, so a lot of people can try it right away.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:50.160
If you have an iPhone, open settings, go to general, then software update, and install iOS 27 when it appears.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:59.320
After it is on, open the new Siri app, and say, remind me to text my friend about the weekend, and notice how the refreshed experience feels.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:06.680
Then set a quiet alarm and drag the system sound slider on its own, just to feel those two knobs working separately.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:17.900
Meanwhile, some people are still meeting chat GPT for the very first time. Chat GPT is a chat bot, which means you type a question in plain language, and it writes a reply.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:27.000
A Reddit user overheard two supermarket workers talking, and one suggested using chat GPT. The other person had never even heard the name.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:35.260
That little scene is a reminder that these tools still spread through ordinary conversations, not because everyone already lives inside them.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:42.820
Awareness is still growing by word of mouth, the same way a good game or a YouTube channel hops from one locker to the next.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:49.000
If you want to see how simple it can be, open any web browser and go to the chat GPT website.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:54.020
Type a normal question like, help me plan a weekend with friends on a small budget.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:06:01.280
No account is needed for the basic version, and the reply comes back in plain sentences you can read or copy right away.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:08.480
Treat it like the world's most patient planning buddy for a school project, except it never gets tired of rewriting the list.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:14.900
Watch whether the plan actually fits a small budget, or whether it sounds fancy and needs a second pass from you.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.840
A couple of smaller notes worth parking in your brain before you go.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:25.260
A new report found that AI chat bots gave wrong financial advice 57% of the time.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.840
Researchers tested common questions people might ask about savings, loans, or investments.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:36.520
That is more than half, like a classmate guessing on a test and still missing most of the answers.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:42.340
Double check anything about money with a real person or a source you already trust before you act on it.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.840
Open AI is also testing clickable ads that start a chat inside chat GPT.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:54.560
Instead of shipping you off to another page, some ads now open a conversation with the AI right in the app.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:07:01.960
You keep talking instead of leaving the screen, like a salesperson who sits down at your table rather than handing you a flyer and walking away.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:08.280
It is an early look at how helpful answers and sponsored suggestions might share the same chat in the future.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:14.280
That's it for today, remember every AI expert started exactly where you are right now.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.760
If something we talked about today may you curious, go try it. That's literally how learning works.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.340
Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we'll see you tomorrow.

